of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =18-{3.5}^{2} \\\\  & =18-12.25 \\\\  & =5.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e448e28-466c-5051-9ada-5e030e6a8ff7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Standard Deviation of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "628c0069-f4dc-53cd-aed0-ecb82d580e1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410451} {:answer/id #uuid "7343a751-cd78-5b59-8011-1e74e9d823c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410452} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3fe6f1-6e29-5dfa-896a-f38bb44b409d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410456} {:answer/id #uuid "e169670d-6976-5ddd-bc4f-8bbaef5c24d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410461} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b9a1a2-e3e4-59b1-8b62-123fabfad613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc3fe6f1-6e29-5dfa-896a-f38bb44b409d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410456} :answer-field/id #uuid "54f3e13c-4881-5f73-95a1-cd084b9b5b78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ddfb506-4076-564a-9cbf-01888893404d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129110" :question/problem "Two fair  four-sided dice are rolled and $X$ is the absolute difference of their scores. The probability mass function $f(x)$ of $X$ is shown in the table below. What is $\\text{SD}[X]?$ \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |" :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a random variable $X$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]},\n$$\n\nwhere the variance can be computed using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{4})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{4})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+4(\\frac{1}{4})+9(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-{(\\frac{5}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{25}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{15}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e6a0c79-9597-5fca-9d41-305c541a7bdf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variance Given a Probability Mass Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "047e735d-3969-505a-9203-00c72a2a1536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410440} {:answer/id #uuid "40d9a509-d081-50a4-b65c-ab3d251ab47f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410447} {:answer/id #uuid "89c3d463-5efb-5519-a3d9-13f042900afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410453} {:answer/id #uuid "a10dddf4-6af0-5fe9-b6c8-1e9bdf070f41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{399}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410454} {:answer/id #uuid "d9fb09aa-f54c-525c-8398-39a7537c8a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{399}{256}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9fb09aa-f54c-525c-8398-39a7537c8a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{399}{256}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410459} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c1ad2dd-49e4-5c02-ac98-f746b50c5d1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "967806ee-7237-5a36-94c7-46285ecfda95" :question/math-academy-id "q-129376" :question/problem "Let $X$ be the number obtained by a spinner with five sections labeled $-2,-1,0,1,2.$ The probability mass function $f(x)$ of $X$ is shown in the table below. What is $\\text{Var}[X]?$\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |" :question/worked-solution "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =(-2)\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =(-2)(\\frac{1}{8})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{4})+0(\\frac{3}{8})+1(\\frac{1}{16})+2(\\frac{3}{16}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & =(-2)^{2}\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)^{2}\\cdot f(-1)+{0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{8})+1(\\frac{1}{4})+0(\\frac{3}{8})+1(\\frac{1}{16})+4(\\frac{3}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{16}-{(-\\frac{1}{16})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{16}-\\frac{1}{256} \\\\  & =\\frac{400}{256}-\\frac{1}{256} \\\\  & =\\frac{399}{256}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "11b6d79a-b13d-5e77-899d-8b1b91c872b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variance Given the Expected Value of a Random Variable and Its Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "123d88b7-9486-5594-8990-9a41d6aa27a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{39}{50}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410442} {:answer/id #uuid "3e2bbc05-907f-5fa2-9ace-d03b3459805d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410446} {:answer/id #uuid "5dfbb2b0-4850-57fe-8e1c-d722559c182b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{71}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410450} {:answer/id #uuid "c23e1601-7810-56cc-855c-b729ce1acc00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410457} {:answer/id #uuid "f787ac39-f172-5118-a383-007f850a6ba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dfbb2b0-4850-57fe-8e1c-d722559c182b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{71}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410450} :answer-field/id #uuid "5db94061-cdf0-57e7-b013-67cd72f1cc89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9682caf0-f7aa-52f6-bd4c-fbe55d6bcce7" :question/math-academy-id "q-84011" :question/problem "If $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{5}$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\\frac{3}{4},$ then what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\frac{3}{4}-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{71}{100}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410474 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e448e28-466c-5051-9ada-5e030e6a8ff7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Standard Deviation of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10210515-50f6-5fd6-8a48-684006b7b4c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410441} {:answer/id #uuid "399366e9-b329-589f-b6b7-c66173898456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410445} {:answer/id #uuid "5ae5a64a-b213-5535-92c5-38a856f25be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410449} {:answer/id #uuid "c554640b-d225-5526-832d-c61f7bfe9dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410458} {:answer/id #uuid "dcd4de70-0442-5c0e-83ef-ae71c8ba8451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c554640b-d225-5526-832d-c61f7bfe9dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410458} :answer-field/id #uuid "02c755b2-7fc7-5fd5-a6c9-1e35ce8c1cf9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9ff9e2b0-8e44-5179-bc73-cbf11e934efb" :question/math-academy-id "q-84312" :question/problem "Two biased coins are tossed several times. The results are recorded below. Based on this data, if the random variable $X$ represents the number of heads obtained on a random toss, what is $\\text{SD}[X]?$\n\n| Number of heads | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Frequency | $4$ | $12$ | $9$ |" :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a random variable $X$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]},\n$$\n\nwhere the variance can be computed using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute the probability mass function $f(x).$ To do this, we divide each frequency by the total, which is $4+12+9=25.$ We get the following result:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{4}{25}$ | $\\frac{12}{25}$ | $\\frac{9}{25}$ |\n\nNow, we compute $\\text{E}[X]$ by summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{4}{25})+1(\\frac{12}{25})+2(\\frac{9}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{4}{25})+1(\\frac{12}{25})+4(\\frac{9}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{25}-{(\\frac{6}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{25}-\\frac{36}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
